==============================================================================
DATA, NOT SCHEDULE - the confound in 20260822-datasize-10contrast.log, split
scored 2026-08-22 by tools/probe_bisect.py --paired --json, one pass per
checkpoint per set, all three in the plain basis (see the note below).

so400m-full moved the mean by +0.040 over so400m-s30k while changing two
things at once: 4x the images AND 2x the epochs. so400m-s30k-e40 is 30 000
images for 40 epochs - the missing cell - trained with everything else held
at the recipe the other two use (batch 512, lr 0.006, infonce 0.3, augment).

run                       book   glass  laptop  refrig    oven  toilet  umbrel  suitca    bowl     bed    mean
so400m-s30k   30k  20ep  0.565   0.600   0.616   0.714   0.604   0.435   0.421   0.646   0.742   0.618   0.596
so400m-s30k-e40 30k 40ep 0.590   0.648   0.575   0.618   0.452   0.373   0.562   0.665   0.762   0.603   0.585
so400m-full  118k  40ep  0.605   0.654   0.722   0.760   0.540   0.382   0.533   0.683   0.774   0.705   0.636

teacher 1152             0.907   0.933   0.781   0.786   0.850   0.579   0.715   0.894   0.819   0.847   0.811
pca 512 (plain)          0.917   0.933   0.775   0.804   0.873   0.595   0.725   0.888   0.866   0.872   0.825

Paired differences over the ten sets, one variable moved at a time:
  epochs alone, 20 -> 40   at 30k    : -0.011 +-0.026
  data alone,   30k -> 118k at 40ep  : +0.051 +-0.020
  both at once (the old number)      : +0.040 +-0.019

So the +0.040 was the data. Doubling the schedule at 30 000 images bought
nothing the eval can see, and the error bar is wide enough that it cannot
even be called a loss - it is a null.

Note on where the two older rows come from. so400m-s30k's row is read from
model/runs/_text_score_select_*.json, which scored it alongside the text
sieve on the same sets; so400m-full's is model/runs/_full_score_so400m-full_*.json.
so400m-s30k-e40 is model/runs/_full_score_so400m-s30k-e40_*.json, and
model/runs/ is gitignored, so the two commands that made it are here instead:

  uv run model/distill.py --split train2017 --epochs 40 \
      --batch 512 --lr 0.006 --infonce 0.3 --subset 30000 \
      --targets model/cache/emb_train2017_SO400M-pca512_s30000.npy \
      --name so400m-s30k-e40

  for s in book glass laptop refrigerator oven toilet umbrella suitcase bowl bed; do
    d=20260822-synth-$s-crop; q=bench/stills/$d/queries.txt
    uv run --script tools/probe_bisect.py \
       --a bench/stills/$d/pos --b bench/stills/$d/neg \
       --pos "$(sed -n 1p $q)" --neg "$(sed -n 2p $q)" \
       --paired --keep bench/stills/$d/keep.txt --runs so400m-s30k-e40 \
       --json model/runs/_full_score_so400m-s30k-e40_$s.json
  done

All three checkpoints were distilled against a plain PCA basis
- emb_train2017_SO400M-pca512{,_s30000}, whose `mu` and `w` are bit-identical
- so the teacher and pca rows are one set of numbers for all three, and the
comparison never crosses a space.

The two -a05 checkpoints are NOT in this table. They live in a differently
whitened basis and belong to the other log.
